    "description": "•\tFully functional and self-directed\n•\tProvide formal mentorship.\n•\tComplete high complexity copy projects.\n•\tOwn best practices for developers.\n•\tProvide feedback and direction to other developers on their work.\n•\tEstablish development standards and templates for primary clients.                                              \n•\tPresent work and other's work directly to the client.\n•\tResponsible for executing approved designs by the creative team, relying on expertise in semantic HTML and CSS including HTML 5 and CSS 3, and JavaScript Libraries like jQuery to code Front-End solutions referencing site maps, wireframes and visual design templates. Experience with responsive design, a good understanding of cross-browser and cross-platform rendering issues, W3C standards, and be proficient in content management systems and most aspects of web design production using Bootstrap. He works with designers to make sure user interaction and visual design ideas are faithfully interpreted and with back end developers to ensure correct implementation of the UI front-end. \n•\tAdapt communication to fit the \"audience\".\n•\tUse direct persuasion, facts and figures appropriately to gain buy-in and compel others to positive action.\n•\tDemonstrate critical thinking/problem solving skills to frame a situation/concept.\n•\tCommunicate effectively downward, laterally and one layer upward.\n•\tBalance company, team, and personal achievement.\n•\tPossess good leadership skills and has the ability to mentor less experienced test associates.\n•\tIdentify conflict and drive to closure.\n",
